{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q421274","formula":"C₁₄H₁₀N₄O₅","hill":"C14H10N4O5","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":10.0,"N":4.0,"O":5.0},"names":{"en":"Dantrolene","ru":"Дантролен","uk":"Дантролен"},"descriptions":{"en":"Dantrolene sodium, sold under the brand name Dantrium among others, is a postsynaptic muscle relaxant that lessens excitation-contraction coupling in muscle cells. It achieves this by inhibiting Ca2+ ions release from sarcoplasmic reticulum stores by antagonizing ryanodine receptors. It is the primary drug used for the treatment and prevention of malignant hyperthermia, a rare, life-threatening disorder triggered by general anesthesia or drugs.","ru":"Дантролен — миорелаксант, механизм действия которого основывается на блокаде рианодиновых рецепторов (кальциевых каналов саркоплазматического ретикулума миоцитов)."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":2952,"mass":314.25,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1C(=O)NC(=O)N1N=CC2=CC=C(O2)C3=CC=C(C=C3)[N+](=O)[O-]","inchikey":"OZOMQRBLCMDCEG-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-[[5-(4-nitrophenyl)furan-2-yl]methylideneamino]imidazolidine-2,4-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"2952","atoms":33,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.228,"y":-0.254,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":-6.099,"y":2.967,"z":0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":-6.093,"y":-1.622,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":7.423,"y":0.306,"z":0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":6.554,"y":2.326,"z":-0.001,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.381,"y":-0.016,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-6.476,"y":0.673,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.325,"y":-0.854,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":6.435,"y":1.078,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.239,"y":1.408,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.242,"y":-1.154,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":2.568,"y":-0.585,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.923,"y":-0.975,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.702,"y":1.81,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.695,"y":-0.466,"z":